	"_comment": "Save-contribution vectors (spec 2026-10-17-pro-downgrade-inert-attributes §3.4, §8 V9). Each vector is a block's name, the attribute names its type registers, its attributes and the props the save already carries; `today` is the saved root element as today's three Pro save filters serialize it (recorded by save-contributions-vectors.test.js with BL_RECORD_VECTORS=1, never typed), and `expected` is what the one save module must write. They are equal except where `contract` names the rule that changes it: S5 (closed value sets, security read F2) and F3 (a contribution applies only when the block's name is in its list AND its type registers the attribute, security read S2). `blocks` and `sets` are the lists and closed sets the contributions read; the test holds `blocks` to the sidecars.",
